The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (res->type != RDMA_RESTRACK_CM_ID || !res_is_user(res))
    res->task = NULL;
```
```c
if (!res->task)
    rdma_restrack_set_task(res, current);
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that `res->task` is explicitly set to `NULL` when the `res` type is not a connection manager ID or when it is not a user resource. This prevents the function from attempting to set the task with an uninitialized value, thus avoiding the general protection fault. By ensuring that `res->task` is properly initialized before it is used, the code becomes more robust and prevents crashes related to uninitialized variables.

